@@ -3,3 +3,21 @@
 The Lakeside Windsurf School teaches windsurfing on the lake from April to October, and rents boards and
 sails to its students and to visitors who bring their own experience. This repository holds the software
 of its booking desk, written in TypeScript with no runtime dependency.
+
+## Rental module
+
+`createRentalService()` (exported from `src/index.ts`) returns an in-memory service:
+
+- `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice })`: `kind` is `'board'` or `'sail'`, `dailyPrice` is in euro cents.
+- `quote({ itemId, start, end })` returns `{ itemId, start, end, total }`.
+- `book({ itemId, start, end })` returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }`.
+
+Rules applied throughout: money is integer euro cents; times are ISO-8601 UTC strings; a period covers
+whole days (`start` and `end` at midnight UTC, `end` being the start of the day after the last day);
+an item cannot be booked for overlapping periods (back-to-back periods are fine). `quote` and `book` throw
+for an unknown item or a disallowed period, and `book` also throws when the item is not free.
+
+Booking ids are sequential (`booking-1`, `booking-2`, ...) so that behaviour stays deterministic.
+Cancellation (no refund less than 24 hours before the start, full refund otherwise) is not implemented yet.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test` (Node 22.18+, which runs TypeScript directly).
